{
  "slug": "habit-tracker-template",
  "category": "planners",
  "name": "Habit Tracker Template",
  "h1": "Habit Tracker Template (Printable PDF and Word)",
  "metaTitle": "Habit Tracker Printable: Free 31-Day PDF & Word Template",
  "metaDescription": "Free printable habit tracker in PDF and Word. Track 12 habits for 31 days on one A4 landscape page, with goal and done columns and a monthly review box.",
  "short": "Track up to 12 habits across 31 days on one landscape page, with goal and done columns and a monthly review.",
  "accent": "#7E22CE",
  "useCases": [
    "Planning",
    "Tracking"
  ],
  "industries": [
    "Personal",
    "Students",
    "Professionals"
  ],
  "date": "2026-11-19",
  "intro": "This habit tracker template fits a full month on one A4 landscape page. There are 12 rows for habits and 31 numbered day boxes, so you can tick off each day you keep a habit. Two short columns at the end hold your monthly goal and the number of days you actually did it, and a review box at the bottom helps you plan next month.",
  "howTo": [
    "Download the PDF to print it straight away, or the Word file if you want to type your habits before printing.",
    "Write the month and year at the top, and cross out any day boxes your month does not have (29, 30 or 31).",
    "Write one habit per row. Start with three to five habits rather than filling all 12 rows.",
    "In the Goal column, write how many days this month you want to do each habit, for example 20 for exercise.",
    "Each evening, tick or colour the box for that day if you did the habit. Leave it blank if you did not.",
    "On the last day, count the ticks, write the total in the Done column and fill in the review box."
  ],
  "guide": [
    {
      "h": "Why a habit tracker works",
      "p": [
        "A habit tracker turns a vague plan like \"read more\" into a row of boxes you can see. Each tick is a small reward, and a growing chain of ticks makes you want to keep it going. Seeing a gap is useful too: it shows which days or weeks are hard, so you can plan around them.",
        "Keep habits small and clear. \"Read 10 pages\" is easier to tick honestly than \"read a lot\". \"Walk 20 minutes\" is easier than \"get fit\"."
      ]
    },
    {
      "h": "Setting a realistic goal for each habit",
      "p": [
        "Not every habit needs to happen every day. Turn how often you want to do it into a number for the month. Exercising every other day in a 30 day month means a goal of 15. Drinking eight glasses of water daily means a goal of 30 or 31. Writing the number in the Goal column lets you judge progress fairly instead of feeling bad about the blank days."
      ]
    },
    {
      "h": "Reviewing your month",
      "p": [
        "At the end of the month, compare Done with Goal for each habit. If you hit the goal easily, raise it a little next month. If you were far below it, make the habit smaller or pick a better time of day. Use the review box to note what helped, what got in the way and the one change you will make. Keep each month's sheet in a folder so you can see your progress over time."
      ]
    }
  ],
  "tips": [
    "Keep the tracker where you will see it every day, such as on the fridge, your desk or inside your diary.",
    "Tick the boxes at the same time each day, for example just before bed.",
    "Link a new habit to something you already do, like stretching right after brushing your teeth.",
    "If you miss a day, try not to miss two in a row.",
    "Use one colour for done and a different mark for days you did a smaller version of the habit."
  ],
  "faqs": [
    {
      "q": "How many habits can I track on this sheet?",
      "a": "There are 12 rows. Most people do better with three to six habits at a time, so use the spare rows only once the first habits feel easy."
    },
    {
      "q": "Can I use it for any month?",
      "a": "Yes. The day boxes are numbered 1 to 31 with no fixed month, so it works for every month and year. Just cross out the days your month does not have."
    },
    {
      "q": "What paper size is it?",
      "a": "A4 landscape. It also prints on US Letter if you choose Fit to page in the print settings."
    },
    {
      "q": "Can I fill it in on my phone?",
      "a": "You can type in the PDF with the free Edit PDF tool on ZentaPDF, but the tracker is designed to be printed and ticked by hand."
    },
    {
      "q": "How do I print trackers for the whole year?",
      "a": "Print the PDF 12 times, or set the number of copies in your print dialog. To keep one digital file, join copies with Merge PDF."
    }
  ],
